% Origin: Kowalski, *Computational Logic and Human Thinking*,
%         Chapter 14 "Logic and Objects", section 14.1
%         ("Extreme Behaviourism: the fox and the crow as input-output objects").
% Last verification: no open issues (no errors/warnings; all tests pass).
%
% The book gives four "if ... then ..." rules describing the fox/crow as
% input-output objects. We rewrite each as Head-if-Body and generalize the
% fox and crow to generic animals. "food" is treated as a single constant.
% Because "the food falls to the ground" does not by itself entail "the food is
% next to fox", we (as suggested) simply supply "the food is next to fox" as a
% scenario fact so the pick-up rule fires.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
*a first animal* sees *a second animal*.
*an animal* has food in its mouth.
*an animal* praises *a second animal*.
*an animal* sings.
the food falls to the ground.
the food is next to *an animal*.
*an animal* picks up the food.

the knowledge base behaviourist fox includes:

% an animal praises a second animal if the (first) animal sees the second animal
% and the second animal has food in its mouth.
a first animal praises a second animal
    if the first animal sees the second animal
    and the second animal has food in its mouth.

% a second animal sings if a first animal praises the second animal.
a second animal sings
    if a first animal praises the second animal.

% the food falls to the ground if an animal has the food in its mouth and the
% animal sings.
the food falls to the ground
    if an animal has food in its mouth
    and the animal sings.

% an animal picks up the food if the food is next to the animal.
an animal picks up the food
    if the food is next to the animal.

scenario story is:
    fox sees crow.
    crow has food in its mouth.
    the food is next to fox.
    singer expects answers ["crow sings"].
    falls expects answers ["the food falls to the ground"].
    picker expects answers ["fox picks up the food"].

query singer is:
    which animal sings.

query falls is:
    the food falls to the ground.

query picker is:
    which animal picks up the food.
